template <typename T>
typename T::value_type top(const T& c) {
    if (!c.empty()) {
        return c.back();  // Safely returns the last element if the container is not empty
    } else {
        // Handle the empty case, e.g., throw an exception to avoid undefined behavior
        throw std::out_of_range("Container is empty");
    }
}

Practical usage notes: Use 'typename T::value_type' to access the container's element type, ensuring the template parameter T (e.g., std::vector<int>) supports operations like empty() and back(). Always check for emptiness before accessing elements to adhere to best practices and avoid common pitfalls like segmentation faults in production code.
